<!--
  profiletool's HAGC FAMILY fixture — a conforming ICC.1 clause 8.10 HDR Profile whose
  headroomAdaptiveGainCurveTag carries FOUR alternate images — the most the encoding allows
  (IccLibXML refuses a fifth) — spread across the whole 0 … 6 stop headroom range, two on
  EACH side of the baseline.

  Why this exists. Every other HAGC fixture in the corpus exercises the tag's LAYOUT
  (common parameters, mixing types, hex authoring, slope forms) with one to three
  curves, and only HagcDisplay has an alternate above its baseline. None of them shows
  what the tag is FOR: a family of tone curves that a CMM blends between as the display
  headroom changes. This one is authored to be looked at — the HAGC evaluated view's
  heatmap, curve family and preview strip — and to pin the blending numerically.

  Layout (baseline 3.0 stops = content mastered for a display 8× the HDR reference white):

      headroom   role                         last control point → output
      0.0        compress to SDR               x 4.0, G −2.00  → 1.000 (= 2^0)
      1.5        compress                      x 8.0, G −1.50  → 2.828 (= 2^1.5)
      3.0        BASELINE — no curve stored, the identity
      4.5        expand                        x 8.0, G +1.00  → 16.0
      6.0        expand                        x 8.0, G +2.00  → 32.0

  Every curve's grey output x·2^G increases strictly through its control points, and each
  compressing curve ends exactly at its own display peak, so above the last point the
  evaluator's clip (G = y_last + log2(x_last/x)) holds the output AT that peak. Signs follow
  the headroom ordering (proposal 0.1.3.6): Y ≤ 0 below the baseline, Y ≥ 0 above it.

  Deliberately uniform so the pictures read cleanly: one mixing type (2) on every
  alternate, so a single gain curve exists at every headroom; PCHIP-derived slopes
  throughout; no custom chromaticities. Layout variety is covered by the upstream
  fixtures.

  Otherwise the same conforming shell as ProfiletoolHdrDisplay: RGB Display v4.50, BT.2020
  primaries adapted to D50, PQ via cicpTag, no TRC tags, identity AToB0/BToA0 pair.
  HDRReferenceWhite 203 agrees with CRWL; DERH 3.0 matches the baseline headroom.

  Generated through the iccxml WASM path (xmlToIcc), not by hand.
-->
